      "message": "It looks like this patch doesn\u0027t change behaviour on its own. aosp/4368058 already bounds `dma_direct_mmap()`, `__dma_mmap_from_coherent()`, `iommu_dma_mmap()` and `dma_mmap_pages()` with `vma_kernel_pages()` and remaps `vma_size(vma)` in place. And since aosp/4368055, `remap_pfn_range()` in a 4KB VMA maps 4KB frames starting at the slice that `vma_slice_offset()` gives the address. So `dma_mmap_pfn()` mostly moves those lines around, which grows the P3S diff against upstream in five core files.\n\nAs far as I can see, the only later patch that changes `dma_mmap_pfn()` is aosp/4368011 (in p3s_6.18_b19), which adds the `vma_is_p3s_4k()` branch. The `-ENXIO` and oversized remap problems that its commit message describes also look like the ones aosp/4368058 fixed.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this patch? If aosp/4368011 is still needed, could you fold this refactor into it, so that `dma_mmap_pfn()` comes with its first user?",
